    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d892">

                <pb facs="0958" n="1792" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1792"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/7098</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-22T16:00:00+01:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 22, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.52 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4057. My 2890, August 8, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d892-f1"/> Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs informs me that according to article 4 of declaration of
                    neutrality war vessels and vessels assimilated thereto, such as armed
                    merchantmen, belonging to belligerent countries are excluded as general rule
                    from the Netherlands territory including colonial possessions. Following
                    exceptions to rule are recognized: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Vessels of above classes may enter Netherlands territorial waters in
                            case of shipwreck or storm; must leave as soon as circumstances
                            permit.</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>Vessels of this description may enter ports of Dutch colonial
                            possessions for sole purpose of completing supply of provision and coal
                            but must leave as soon as purpose has been accomplished and at any rate
                            within 24 hours.</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>Such vessels if destined for a religious, scientific, or philanthropic
                            mission are not affected by rule of exclusion.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
